WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:01.742
AYSYLU GREENBERG: Hi, everyone.

00:00:01.742 --> 00:00:05.880
I'm Aysylu Greenberg, and I'm
here at Kubecon San Diego 2019.

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:08.170
I'm a senior software
engineer at Google.

00:00:08.170 --> 00:00:11.080
And today, I gave a talk
on Binary Authorization

00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:12.390
in Kubernetes.

00:00:12.390 --> 00:00:14.590
It was a joint talk
with Liron Levin,

00:00:14.590 --> 00:00:17.120
who is one of the biggest
contributors to both Grafeas

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:18.570
and Kritis projects.

00:00:18.570 --> 00:00:21.120
And we discussed how
Grafeas and Kritis

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:23.730
can help you secure your
software supply chain.

00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:26.340
If you are not familiar with the
term "software supply chain,"

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:27.870
it's basically
all the steps that

00:00:27.870 --> 00:00:31.350
take you through committing
the code to the code base,

00:00:31.350 --> 00:00:34.710
and then building it and testing
it using continuous integration

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:37.240
pipelines, and then deploying
it to Kubernetes using

00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:38.820
continuous delivery pipeline.

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:41.730
And in this talk,
we also discussed

00:00:41.730 --> 00:00:44.250
how to populate the
data into Grafeas--

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:48.120
Liron showed a nice demo of the
Twistlock populating the data--

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:49.890
and then deploying
that to Kubernetes

00:00:49.890 --> 00:00:53.130
and using Kritis to actually
gain the deployment, depending

00:00:53.130 --> 00:00:56.780
on whether you found critical
vulnerabilities or not.

00:00:56.780 --> 00:00:59.220
So if you came to the
talk, thank you very much.

00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:01.020
If you haven't seen
it yet, I highly

00:01:01.020 --> 00:01:03.070
recommend you check it
out when it's online.

00:01:03.070 --> 00:01:06.480
And please come by the Google
booth at Kubecon San Diego.

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:07.040
Thank you.

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:09.790
[MUSIC PLAYING]

